@startuml
!include theme.iuml
title Camfranglais — target deployment and private persistence
top to bottom direction
node "Visitor device\nDesktop or mobile browser" as Browser
cloud "HTTPS Internet\ncamfranglais.duckdns.org" as Internet
node "Ubuntu 24.04 VPS — 109.199.120.38" as VPS {
  node "Nginx\n80: redirect to TLS\n443: HTTPS reverse proxy" as Nginx
  node "systemd: camfranglais.service\nservice user: camfranglais" as Systemd {
    node "Uvicorn / FastAPI\n127.0.0.1:2021 only" as App
  }
  artifact "/var/www/francanglaiscompiler\nPython source + frontend/dist" as Code
  artifact "/etc/camfranglais.env\nrestricted operator configuration" as Env
  folder "/var/lib/camfranglais\nrestricted persistent data" as Data {
    database "shared-workspace/workspace.sqlite3" as Workspace
    database "public-access.sqlite3" as Limits
    folder "shared-workspace/audio + backups" as Media
    database "auth.sqlite3 / legacy workspaces\npreserved, not publicly served" as Legacy
  }
}
actor "Server operator" as Operator
Browser --> Internet : TLS requests / responses
Internet --> Nginx : 443
Nginx --> App : private loopback proxy\ntrusted forwarded scheme/address
App ..> Code : executable code / same-origin static assets
Systemd ..> Env : EnvironmentFile
App --> Workspace
App --> Limits
App --> Media
Operator ..> Code : controlled release update
Operator ..> Data : private backup / recovery
Operator ..> Env : deployment configuration
note bottom of App
  Default release design: public_read_only.
  Production requires the built frontend and a public HTTPS origin.
  SMTP and Google credentials are not required in public mode.
  Do not expose :2021 as a public application URL.
end note
legend bottom
  This is the intended deployment of the final source, not evidence that an update was executed.
  Last supplied remote observation (26 September): HTTPS health 200; bootstrap 401 from the old deployment.
  A prepared updater is not proof of a remotely installed release. Re-check bootstrap after deployment.
  Operator recovery must preserve data/configuration; a workspace ZIP does not recreate account identities.
endlegend
@enduml
